hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to an  edition of ask Evan today I'm gonna  answer a question from one of my  newsletter readers magdelena who wrote  in about trying to figure out how to  market herself better online so she  wrote insane  hi Evan I'm so grateful for having the  opportunity to get this powerful  business connection I moved to Florida  less than three years ago I've been in  helping wellness for over 18 years and  I've had my own business for 16 years I  work as a massage therapist and a  wellness practitioner and a wholeness  holistic coach I want to take my  business to a whole new level I've  started a new blog my biggest challenge  is marketing my business and myself and  getting known on the platform just  thinking about this idea and taking the  next step can be overwhelming thank you  for your willingness to help others in  business best wishes magdalena so thanks  to the question Congrats them haven't  encouraged to go out and start something  new it is a big challenge especially if  you're not technically savvy I know it  can be hard to set up online and get a  blog going and it can feel very  overwhelming so don't freak out there  are easy ways to kind of take small  steps to get yourself going if you are  using a platform like WordPress and be  really easy to post and make updates and  not feel like you're always at the mercy  of somebody who knows a lot more from  the technology side a point of view but  to answer your question on how to get  more well-known a couple of ideas for  you the first I would try to look at  guest blogging so this is a really  common way to get yourself more  well-known you basically call up our  email or get in touch with other people  who have blogs who are in your industry  so other people who are talking about  health and wellness or holistic care and  offer to write them a guest post and it  helps to have a couple topics in mind or  give them some samples or show them some  of your really best a really good posts  on your own site and then from there  offer to write a great post for them and  then link back to your site so the idea  here is you're making partnerships with  people who already have an audience you  can connect with and then have them help  promote you as well and you can get new  readers and then get them hopefully  signed up to subscribe to your blog as  well so that's a great way to get  started and usually blog owners are open  to the idea of having guest posting just  because  especially as they've had a blog for a  while it can be hard to keep content  current right it's hard to come up with  ideas all the time so having people who  are creating quality content not just  promotional pieces but really good stuff  can be a big boost to help them out as  well so that could be a good short-term  relationship but also long-term you can  contribute on an ongoing basis as well  to help drive traffic and awareness back  to your site the second thing I would do  is try to get some media so I use a  service called PR leads there are other  free services you can use as well or you  can just try to find local reporters or  online reporters who cover your space  basically idea here is you've done this  for 16 years or 18 years you know what  you're doing right it's not like you're  just starting something out from scratch  ideally as an entrepreneur you are an  expert in your field right why are you  gonna where are people gonna buy your  product or services because you know  what you're talking about so a great way  to get more exposure is to be seen as  that expert for the media so you want to  get on the radar of reporters who are  covering your space now I said I use PR  leads basically what that is the service  it's $99 a month I have no affiliation  with them other than I'm a happy  customer and you get leads from  reporters who are looking for experts  for stories it's a great opportunity to  get into media got me into the near  times and Forbes and a whole bunch of  other places but short of that you can  also create your own list and you can  try to find people who are covering  these kinds of topics and email them on  a regular basis with new story ideas or  comment on stories you've already put up  and the idea here is you want to  showcase yourself as the expert so the  next time they have a story they're  gonna come and talk to you with  reporters with any story that they  create they always want to have an  expert opinion with it right so why  can't that expert be you if you are  credible expert and you know what you're  talking about you're actually making the  reporters lives easier so you really  want to make sure you're targeting in on  a set of reporters who really focus on  your industry and get them to know you  so that's the second one so first is  guest blog and the second is get media  the third thing I would do is try to  start answering people quest people's  questions so just like I make these  youtube videos people ask me questions  and I start answering them these are  questions from my own community so you  are on my newsletter list and asking the  question so I responded if you don't  have a community yet the best question  ants are the ones around the people who  are attached to you but if you don't  have that community yet a great way to  build it is to go out and start  answering people's questions who haven't  heard of you before so I do some  research on Twitter for example I look  at forums that are related to this I  look at YouTube comments see what  questions people are asking and then  create a response for them and it could  be in the form of a blog post on your  site it could be in the form of a video  posts like this if you're comfortable in  front of the camera you could do a  podcast you can do a screencast whatever  it is you're basically answering  somebody's question if somebody has that  same question if you have lots of other  people who have the question as well and  so it shows that you're a responsive  that you know what you're talking about  hopefully you you know have some good  answers for them and then ideally as you  start building this series up you're  gonna be able to get people asking  questions directly to use instead of  just answering a random question on  Twitter or in a format and see people  are gonna start asking you questions and  you get seen as out authority figure and  people are gonna keep going back and  asking more and more questions so it's a  great way to build up if you're writing  the blog it could be you know every  Friday it's ask Magdalena and you're  answering somebody's question and the  start again is somebody else's community  but as hopefully you build up your  presence online you're able to talk to  your own people or could also be from  your your offline base so people who are  your current customers you can say here  are some frequently asked questions that  I get asked and you can create a post  around it or a video or a podcast  whatever it is so hopefully that helps I  know it can be a struggle and can seem  very overwhelming at the start to get  this thing launched remember to take  baby steps do something every day to  move it forward and then it suddenly  becomes less scary when it's this huge a  big project it's easy to get overwhelmed  and have that fear but as you start  getting into something even though it's  brand new it becomes easier and easier  the more you do it so just get started  again and look at trying to do guest  blogging try to get in with the media  and also try to answer people's  questions from different journeys online  so thanks for watching guys if you liked  the video please give it a thumbs up it  makes you want to do more of these  videos for  you and if you have a question about how  to get noticed online or different  question about your business feel free  to leave it in the comment section below  I always try to read those and try to  comment back as much as I can so thank  you and I'll see you on the next episode
 

